#N canvas 20 20 3650 2120 12;
#X declare -lib pdlua;
#X text 20 20 u_tempo -- the master reference: the master BPM \, the pulse oscillator MIDI clock is cut from \, and the transport. Not the clock: anything that needs a beat owns a c_clock. ref/module/tempo.md, f 58;
#X text 20 140 creation args: none. inlet: tap \, from u_map's arrangement row \, the nanoKONTROL's LOOP \, tempo <bpm> \, the phone's \, from u_net \, fast <1 or 0> \, the 500 BPM repeat \, from c_steps \, and rush <x> <live> \, knob 4 \, from u_map. outlet 1: the master BPM \, clamped \, whenever the tempo bus carries one \, to u_net. outlet 2: the BPM a tap \, the phone or a section set \, to u_map \, which holds knob 1 there. outlet 3: rush <bpm> \, knob 4 past the handoff \, to c_steps. It talks on tempo \, clock \, start \, stop \, panic \, disp \, err and state \, the tempo being the playing section's \, and out of two MIDI ports: port 1 carries the clock and the transport \, and port 4 takes panic's STOP alone. Port 3 gets nothing., f 80;
