#X text 20 1160 Audio-domain buys a phase-continuous rate change and one phase that grain code can read. It does not reduce the 1.45 ms jitter on the outgoing byte \, which vanilla Pd cannot fix., f 58;
#X text 20 1360 The counter resets to 23 \, so the next pulse lands on 0 \, the beat. Reset to 0 \, the first beat after every start is skipped., f 58;
#X text 780 1160 Clock never stops: 248 flows whether the transport runs or not \, or a device following it stretches to whatever tempo it last measured., f 44;
#X text 780 1330 Never 251: nothing in this rig has Song Position Pointer., f 44;
#X text 780 1460 panic sends 252 to ports 1 and 4 \, lights the aux LED and leaves the clock running. Port 4 only here \, since a Volca sequencing through a panic is the case it exists for (item 279). Silencing notes is each device layer's., f 44;
#X text 1450 870 The loadbang's del 200 publishes 120 on tempo once \, if nothing has yet: the fallback (the spigot \, right). The tempo is not drawn at rest: the OLED is for alerts \, levels and a control's name as it moves \, and the phone shows the tempo (ref/module/tempo.md)., f 44;
#X text 1450 1070 It stores what it hears and never re-emits \, so there is no loop with the bus., f 44;
#X text 300 1000 Three receives on one name \, all into cold inlets \, so their order does not matter., f 44;
#X text 620 1000 A 0 in threshold~'s right inlet forces it low \, so a start with the phasor above 0.5 does not wait for a wrap., f 30;
#X text 1450 1250 Debounces are 0: threshold~ counts dead time in blocks \, so any debounce loses pulses at speed (item 58 \, ref/module/tempo.md)., f 44;
#X obj 1900 370 spigot 1;
#X obj 2280 225 r tempo;
#X obj 2280 270 t b;
#X msg 2280 315 0;
#X text 2280 380 The 120 is a fallback: it races mother's knob push \, so any tempo closes the spigot and the seed only fills a silence. With nothing Saved it is the tempo \, since u_map holds knob 1 at this same 120 (R.UNSAVED in u_map.lua \, ref/module/tempo.md)., f 50;
#X msg 1220 990 252;
#X obj 1220 1035 s \$0-rt4;
#X text 620 1810 The same 252 on a receive nothing else writes \, so no clock byte can reach the port-4 box. It fires first \, off the panic trigger's rightmost outlet: the Volca is the longest path in the rig., f 44;
