#X text 3000 1400 Rush \, knob 4 (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): from u_map \, rush <x> <live> \, with the BPM in force added \, as fast has it. The Lua sends its BPMs straight to the tempo bus by its fifth outlet \, not through t f f \, since u_map holds knob 1 itself as it passes knob 4 on \, with the put shut as for the 500 BPM repeat. Past the handoff how far goes to c_steps \, outlet 4 here \, which has the loop. The Lua's eighth outlet is a BPM to hold the knobs at without touching the bus \, when the saved tempo's pad ends rush. ref/module/tempo.md, f 50;
